# Requests for the IntercomEventing Minimal API sample (dotnet run --project Samples/IntercomEventing.Samples.WebApi).
# Watch the live feed while sending them:  curl -N http://localhost:5281/events/stream

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5281

### Place an order: IntercomEvent<OrderPlaced>. The response waits for the handlers (the confirmation mail takes ~200 ms)
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerEmail": "ada@example.com", "sku": "MN-27", "quantity": 2 }

### An order whose confirmation fails: the handler's exception is logged by DefaultExceptionHandler, the order still succeeds
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerEmail": "nobody@example.invalid", "sku": "KB-01", "quantity": 1 }

### List the orders
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders

### Day's sales against the goal: ThresholdEvent raises DailySalesGoalReached once, on the order that crosses 500
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/sales

### Start a new sales day: resets the running total without raising, so the goal can be reached again
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders/sales/new-day

### Pause the store: StateChangeEvent raises once; sending the same status again returns "changed": false
PUT {{baseUrl}}/store/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "Paused", "reason": "Stock count" }

### Orders are rejected while the store is not open
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerEmail": "ada@example.com", "sku": "MS-02", "quantity": 1 }

### Reopen the store
PUT {{baseUrl}}/store/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "Open", "reason": "Stock count finished" }

### Change a price: visible at once in /products
PUT {{baseUrl}}/products/KB-01/price
Content-Type: application/json

{ "price": 79.00 }

### Change another price within 2 seconds: DebounceEvent coalesces both into one price-list publish
PUT {{baseUrl}}/products/MS-02/price
Content-Type: application/json

{ "price": 34.00 }

### Current catalog
GET {{baseUrl}}/products

### Published price list: updates about 2 seconds after the last price change
GET {{baseUrl}}/products/price-list

### Audit: the custom BatchEvent writes entries in batches of 5, and a TimedEvent flushes a partial batch every 15 seconds
GET {{baseUrl}}/audit

### Write the waiting audit entries now
POST {{baseUrl}}/audit/flush
